# The build context is the Go module and nothing else. Everything listed here is
# either not needed to produce the binary, or must not end up in an image layer.

# Version control. Excluded because the history is large, is not needed to
# build, and would otherwise be readable inside any layer that copied it. The
# Dockerfile passes -buildvcs=false for the same reason.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# Documentation and process notes. Not inputs to a build.
docs
CLAUDE.md
README.md

# Test material. testdata/vectors.json is a shipped deliverable for other
# implementations to verify against (§9), not something the binary reads: it is
# embedded nowhere and opened only by tests.
testdata
**/*_test.go

# Deployment artefacts. The image does not build itself, and .env holds the
# operator's domain.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
Caddyfile
.env
.env.example

# Local runtime state. A directory's database holds only ciphertext, but it has
# no business in a build context regardless — and copying one in would seed the
# image with somebody's records.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
data
dist

# Local build and test output.
trigstationd
trigstationd.exe
*.test
*.test.exe
*.out
coverage.txt

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
